  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total number of acorns that Shawna, Sheila, and Danny have altogether, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of acorns Sheila has.\n2. Calculate the number of acorns Danny has.\n3. Sum the acorns of Shawna, Sheila, and Danny.\n\nFirst, we know that Shawna has 7 acorns. Sheila has 5 times as many acorns as Shawna. Therefore, we calculate the number of acorns Sheila has as follows:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of acorns Sheila has} = 5 \\times 7 = 35\n\\]\n\nNext, we know that Sheila has 3 fewer acorns than Danny. Therefore, we can find the number of acorns Danny has by adding 3 to the number of acorns Sheila has:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of acorns Danny has} = 35 + 3 = 38\n\\]\n\nNow, we sum the acorns of Shawna, Sheila, and Danny to find the total number of acorns:\n\\[\n\\text{Total number of acorns} = 7 + 35 + 38 = 80\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of acorns they have altogether is \\boxed{80}.",
